# Secrets — NEVER commit this
.env

# NOTE: certs/aiven-ca.pem IS committed on purpose. It is Aiven's PUBLIC
# CA certificate (used only to verify TLS) — not a credential. Committing
# it means every machine/CI runner can verify the DB connection without
# manual setup. The actual DB password lives only in .env (ignored above).

